c01-headline = Bar settings unavailable
c01-description = Orbit couldn't open this bar's settings, so its corners can't be changed. Log out and back in, then try again.
c01-why = The settings store for this bar couldn't be opened.

c02-headline = Bar not found
c02-description = The slider may not match the bar. Turn it on in Settings › Desktop, then reopen this menu.
c02-why = The bar's corner radius couldn't be read. This usually means the bar is turned off or has never been set up.

c03-headline = Corners didn't change
c03-description = The new radius wasn't saved. Try again. If it keeps happening, report it.
c03-why = Writing border_radius to the bar's settings failed.

c04-headline = Your choice wasn't remembered
c04-description = The corners changed, but they may go back the next time Roundness changes or you log in. Try again.
c04-why = Saving the applet's own settings (com.studio72f.OrbitCorners) failed.

c05-headline = Theme settings unavailable
c05-description = Orbit couldn't open the theme's settings, so theme corners can't be changed. The dock and panel still work. Log out and back in, then try again.
c05-why = One of the theme's settings stores (Dark, Light or their Builders) couldn't be opened.

c06-headline = Theme corners didn't change
c06-description = The new radius wasn't saved to every theme. Try again. If it keeps happening, report it.
c06-why = Reading or writing corner_radii in one of the theme's settings stores failed.
